WEBVTT

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:04.980
I have sad news today.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:13.340
This is the final episode of Nico Smiley's 
Dazzling Last Episode Recap Corner!

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:20.480
That's because we've reached 
the final of the four matches

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.300
that I produced for Yuya!

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.120
His opponent is Noboru Gongenzaka!

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.280
He is Yuya's best friend!

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.350
Yuya is flustered because he's 
battling against a friend

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.150
who has always supported him.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.250
But Gongenzaka is also risking his entry

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:44.380
into the Junior Youth 
Championship in this match.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.580
Yuya feels very conflicted.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:52.330
That's when Gongenzaka did 
something no one expected:

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:55.800
He Synchro Summoned!

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:04.520
Well, my time is up.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.680
Please keep watching to 
see what happens next.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.740
Adieu!

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:16.190
Implementing mass into Solid 
Vision has created Action Duels.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:21.050
In duels where the field, monsters 
and duelists become one,

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:24.060
the people are caught in 
a frenzy of excitement!

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.370
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:47.150
You!  The strongest card 
isn't about winning or losing

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:50.560
You!  At full speed  On the game

00:01:57.610 --> 00:01:59.300
Swinging ma ma ma mind

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:03.870
The soul's pendulum  Ultimate confusion

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:06.070
Impulse  Got it got it

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:11.280
Tough battles  Real revolution

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:22.040
Everybody goin'  Break through the walls!

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:28.960
Infinite future  Get rid of indecision!

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.900
Make it Make it  Be courageous (Break it now)

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:36.300
Step ahead!  Take a step (Do it now)

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:46.580
The fun is only getting started!  
So everyone's a Believer!!

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.920
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:59.960
New Territory  Superheavy 
Samurai Warlord Susanowo

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.230
Gongenzaka Synchro Summoned?

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:12.940
Impressive, Gongenzaka!

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:19.320
Yuya...

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.160
Here I go, Yuya.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:26.000
The real match now begins!

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:27.750
Prepare yourself!

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.720
Stop right there!

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.800
My son Noboru has lost this match!

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.360
Gongenzaka lost?

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:39.870
Why?

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:44.980
An unwavering heart is the crucial 
part of the Immovable Duel!

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:49.840
You lost the moment you stole a technique 
from a different style in order to win!

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.400
I didn't steal it!

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.050
I learned it!

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:58.120
Learned it?  You mean from...

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.920
From Yaiba Toudou.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.400
LDS's?

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.520
From an opponent who tormented you?

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:11.760
Even if he's the enemy, it's natural 
to ask for help when I need it.

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:16.980
I didn't learn Synchro 
Summon just so I could win!

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.010
I want to create opportunities 
for a new Immovable Duel!

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:22.740
New Immovable Duel?

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.000
Dueling evolves everyday!

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.800
If Immovable Duel doesn't change,

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:32.580
it will be left behind 
in the next generation!

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:38.540
I want you to make a decision 
after you watch this match!

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:43.390
Superheavy Samurai Warlord Susanowo 
can use its defense points

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:46.600
to attack while in defense position!

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.670
Let's battle!  Go, Susanowo!

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:55.410
Attack Performapal Silver Claw!

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:58.140
Kusanagi Sword Slash!

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.110
Action Spell Evasion!

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.080
It negates your attack!

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.720
I won't let you!

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:10.090
When Susanowo is in defense position and 
there are no spell cards in the graveyard,

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:16.710
I can pay 500 life points to use 
a spell card in your graveyard.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:21.670
I activate the Action Spell Over Sword!

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:31.320
He can activate a spell 
card in Yuya's graveyard?

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.110
But even if he raises its attack points,

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:37.320
it's meaningless because it's using 
its defense points to attack.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:41.000
Actually, Over Sword has another effect.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.050
It's...

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:47.160
When this effect targets my monster, 
you can't negate its attack!

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.900
I end my turn!

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:58.220
Bravo!

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:02.620
This collaboration shows his understanding 
of Action Cards and Synchro Monsters.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:06.720
This may be the birth 
of a new Immovable Duel!

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:11.520
That was incredible.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:15.820
I'm surprised that you 
mastered Synchro this well.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:19.960
After what you've shown me, 
I can't keep losing either!

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:22.060
My turn!  I draw!

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:30.370
I finally found an answer.

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:36.210
Pendulum Fusion.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:38.130
Yuya...

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:44.420
I no longer have Polymerization in my deck.

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:51.860
But I decided to use it as a hint to 
discover what's beyond Pendulum by myself!

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:54.310
What I can do is...

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:00.320
I set the Pendulum Scale

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:04.700
with Scale 2 Performapal Camelump 
and Scale 6 Performapal Lizardraw!

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.750
Swing, my soul's pendulum!

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:19.720
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:21.480
Pendulum Summon!

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:24.180
Come out, my monsters!

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:28.240
Stargazer Magician from my hand!

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:32.980
Performapal Silver Claw from my Extra Deck!

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:39.400
He Pendulum Summoned!

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.160
I'm getting shivers!

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:44.380
But Stargazer and Silver Claw 
are both in defense position.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:45.340
Why?

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:48.810
Gon's Susanowo has 3800 defense points.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:53.420
Yuya doesn't have a monster 
that can destroy it.

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:57.650
So he placed his monsters in 
defense position to form a wall.

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:59.260
That's right.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:02.230
But he can't win like that.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:13.070
I need to think of a new 
way to summon Rune-Eyes.

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:16.040
I end my turn!

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:19.120
All he could do was strengthen his defense.

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:25.080
Maybe Yuya should have held on to this.

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:31.140
Yuya, even if you strengthen your 
defense, there's no time left for you!

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:34.090
My turn!  I draw!

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:40.800
I summon Superheavy Samurai 
Soulpiercer from my hand!

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:45.250
I equip it on Superheavy 
Samurai Warlord Susanowo!

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:53.600
Due to Soulpiercer's effect, when Susanowo 
attacks a monster in defense position,

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:55.430
you take piercing damage!

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:56.570
What?

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:58.320
Battle, Susanowo!

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:00.520
Attack Silver Claw!

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.400
Silver Claw has 700 defense points.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.010
If it's hit with Susanowo's 
3800 attack points...

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:10.010
He'll take 3100 points of damage!

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:12.800
Yuya only has 2000 life 
points, so he'll lose!

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:18.200
Soulpiercer, fire!

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:24.580
I activate the Action Spell Miracle!

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:28.550
My monster's destruction is negated, 
and battle damage is halved!

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.890
I end my turn!

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:43.140
He managed to survive by a hair, but...

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:46.370
Yuya only has 450 life points left.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:48.900
He has two cards in his hand.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.860
The next draw will determine everything.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:53.550
Yuya...

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:04.550
You're truly strong, Gongenzaka.

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:06.560
Are you admitting defeat?

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:08.450
Are you thinking of surrendering?

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:09.720
No.

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:14.060
Even if I do lose, I'll make sure 
you deal the finishing blow.

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:19.260
But that'll only happen after 
I use up all my strength!

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:20.970
My turn!

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:25.120
I can Pendulum Summon!

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:27.910
Come out, my monsters!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:31.500
Level 3 Performapal Hip Hippo!

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:34.550
He now summons...

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:35.810
Hippo?

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:41.840
Performapal Hip Hippo counts as two 
monsters when Tribute Summoning.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:45.060
I tribute Hip Hippo!

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:49.230
I Tribute Summon Odd-Eyes 
Pendulum Dragon from my hand!

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:58.500
It appeared!

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:00.610
Yuya's ace monster!

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:03.870
But since Odd-Eyes has 2500 attack points,

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:07.120
it can't defeat Susanowo 
with 3800 defense points.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:09.310
What are you planning to do, Yuya?

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:11.440
What I can do is...

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:16.290
I activate Performapal 
Lizardraw's Pendulum Effect!

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:23.420
I draw one card from my deck, and 
then I return this card to my deck.

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:29.880
This is everything I can 
do right now!  I draw!

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:34.950
This is...

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:43.100
I place Scale 4 Performapal Trump 
Witch in the Pendulum Zone!

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:48.000
That's pointless!

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:52.660
Even if you do that, you can only 
Pendulum Summon once per turn!

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:56.860
Performapal Trump Witch's 
Pendulum Effect activates!

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:02.080
Once per turn, I can Fusion Summon 
using monsters on my field!

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:09.140
What?

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:11.180
He's using a Pendulum Monster's effect...

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:13.050
...to Fusion Summon?

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:18.680
I fuse Stargazer Magician and 
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:22.720
The one who controls mysterious power,

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:26.290
transform into dazzling light 
and reside in the dragon's eye!

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:27.890
Fusion Summon!

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:31.540
Come out, the sky dragon 
that wields secret arts!

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.420
Rune-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:43.080
Yuya brought out a Fusion Monster!

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:45.520
Hooray!  He did it!

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:47.860
He Fusion Summoned without 
using Polymerization!

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:50.050
I'm shivering too much!

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:53.060
That's Yuya's Fusion Monster?

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:57.620
He's incredible.  Yuya once 
again exceeded my expectations.

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:00.550
Yuya...

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:05.600
Let's battle!

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:09.280
Rune-Eyes Pendulum Dragon, attack Susanowo!

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:15.320
Performapal Camelump's 
Pendulum Effect activates!

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:17.820
It lowers Susanowo's defense points by 800,

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:20.780
and Rune-Eyes deals piercing damage!

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:26.790
Fire!  Shiny Burst!

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:32.980
It's no use!

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:35.390
Even if you lower Susanowo's 
defense points to 3000,

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:38.610
it won't budge if you attack 
with 3000 attack points.

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:40.140
Are you sure about that?

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:40.970
What?

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:45.290
The number of times Rune-Eyes can attack

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:50.810
depends on the Level of the Spellcaster-Type 
monster used to Fusion Summon it.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:54.650
Level 5 Stargazer Magician 
was used to summon Rune-Eyes,

00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:57.620
so Rune-Eyes can attack three times!

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:00.860
Each time it attacks,

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:06.030
Camelump's effect lowers Susanowo's 
defense points by 800.

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:14.430
Go!  Attack for the second time!

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:16.900
Continuous Shiny Burst!

00:14:16.900 --> 00:14:20.800
By paying 500 life points, Susanowo's effect

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.910
lets me activate the Action 
Card Evasion in your graveyard!

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:28.350
It negates your attack!

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:31.280
Very clever!  Good, Noboru!

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:33.020
I'm not done!

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:36.700
Due to Camelump's effect, it 
loses 800 more defense points!

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:42.960
Attack for the third time, Rune-Eyes!

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:44.830
Continuous Shiny Burst!

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.100
He did it!

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:50.460
Finally Susanowo...

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:51.500
...is destroyed!

00:14:51.860 --> 00:14:53.240
Whatever!

00:14:53.240 --> 00:15:00.060
I send Superheavy Samurai Soulbeads from my 
hand to the graveyard to activate its effect!

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:03.920
I can Special Summon a destroyed 
monster in attack position!

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:06.200
Well done again!

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:08.650
Nice recovery, Noboru!

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:14.700
Just when he finally destroyed it...

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:17.460
Gongenzaka is tough.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:21.570
Yuya only has 450 life points, 
so he has to win this turn.

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:24.540
To be honest, that'll be tough.

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:26.940
I can't stay here any longer!

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:27.560
Yeah!

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:29.510
Let's cheer for him up close!

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:30.910
But...

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:32.040
It's fine.

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:36.000
He's focused on the duel.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:39.400
He's overcome the hurdle of an away game.

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:40.490
Ma'am...

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:43.310
You're like a wall.

00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:46.500
A giant wall that's blocking my way.

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:50.930
In order to defeat you, I 
have to overcome my limits.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:56.620
I have to use the card that 
I set at the beginning.

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:01.460
Yuya!

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:02.710
Do your best!

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:06.940
Yuya's only hope is...

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:09.780
...Action Cards scattered around the field.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:24.130
I'll surpass my limits!

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:27.100
He flew?

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:28.530
Yuya!

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:49.320
Yuya, you're such a...

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:52.020
All right!

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:56.430
I send the Action Spell 
Over Sword to the graveyard

00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:59.270
to activate the trap card Danger Draw!

00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:05.500
Due to Danger Draw's effect, I draw one card.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.840
But if the card I draw is a monster,

00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:12.080
I take damage equal to its attack points!

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:14.940
What?

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:19.820
If he draws a monster with 
at least 450 attack points...

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:22.370
...Yuya loses immediately?

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:24.720
Yuya!

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:27.430
He's betting on this draw

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:32.700
whether he can keep going further 
or if everything ends here.

00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:41.810
I believe in myself and my cards!

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:44.910
I draw!

00:17:49.820 --> 00:17:58.060
The Quick-Play Spell Big Return lets me use 
my card's "once per turn" effect again!

00:17:58.370 --> 00:17:59.710
I activate it!

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:03.400
I use Trump Witch's Pendulum Effect!

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:14.710
I Fusion Summon using Performapal Silver 
Claw and Rune-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:15.680
What?

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:16.920
Another...

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:18.080
...Fusion?

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:20.520
Proud silver wolf,

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:24.320
become one with the dragon from the 
heavens to give birth to a new power!

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:26.570
Fusion Summon!

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:30.620
Come out, the ferocious dragon 
with glowing beastly eyes!

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:34.940
Beast-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:52.180
Beast-Eyes Pendulum Dragon, attack 
Superheavy Samurai Warlord Susanowo!

00:18:52.180 --> 00:18:54.210
Hell Dive Burst!

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:06.660
Beast-Eyes Pendulum 
Dragon's effect activates!

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:09.370
When it destroys your monster in battle,

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:13.500
you take damage equal to the attack 
points of the Beast-Type monster

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:15.280
used to Fusion Summon it!

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:19.680
Silver Claw has 1800 attack points!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:23.180
This is the end, Gongenzaka!

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:39.380
Yuya!

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:43.920
You guys?

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:45.000
You won!

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:46.140
Incredible!

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:47.660
I got shivers!

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.060
You were watching?

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:52.600
Yeah!  Nico said that we 
couldn't cheer for you today.

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:54.540
So we hid and watched!

00:19:54.760 --> 00:19:59.010
If you're going to become a pro, 
you have to win away games too.

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:00.320
Mom!

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:02.620
And you won!

00:20:02.620 --> 00:20:04.260
I'm fired up, Yuya!

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:06.360
My blood is boiling!

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:09.480
Even I got a bit excited.

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:12.960
I can't believe you used a 
Pendulum Effect to Fusion Summon.

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:15.930
Yuya, congratulations.

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:17.440
I see.

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:22.140
Even though I didn't know, they 
were still watching over me.

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:25.870
Gongenzaka...

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:31.840
Since I won, you can't enter 
the Junior Youth Championship.

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:33.360
Don't worry.

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:35.020
There's still a week until the tournament.

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:36.580
I still have a chance.

00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:42.320
I'll never forget that I was able 
to battle you with all my strength.

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:50.240
I'm touched!

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:51.800
This is friendship between men-

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:53.770
Dad, you're being annoying!

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:56.480
Noboru, well done!

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:59.560
You two are wonderful duelists!

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:03.000
Well done, Yuya.

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:06.750
You truly are the duelist 
that I expected you'd be.

00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:13.980
You will become a pro like Yusyo 
Sakaki and a first-rate star.

00:21:15.360 --> 00:21:19.780
It's confirmed that Yuya Sakaki will 
enter the Junior Youth Championship.

00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:20.940
I see.

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:26.070
Now all the duelists I 
want are participating.

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:27.200
Yes.

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:32.300
In regards to Masumi Koutsu, Yaiba 
Toudou and Hokuto Shijima...

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:34.810
Have you finished erasing their memories?

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:35.960
Yes.

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:39.050
We erased their duel against Syun Kurosaki,

00:21:39.050 --> 00:21:42.350
and we also erased every detail 
about him up to that point.

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:43.600
Good.

00:21:44.060 --> 00:21:47.780
That means Kurosaki can 
participate in the tournament.

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:51.520
Let's find out how well he can do.

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:55.900
The same goes for them.

00:21:58.400 --> 00:22:06.040
How many of these duelists can become 
spears that will fight for our world?

00:22:13.460 --> 00:22:18.940
Catch the dream dancing in my heart
Release my falling tears

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:28.420
I'll step out on to my first field
To meet my miracle  Fabulous One Step

00:22:35.310 --> 00:22:40.430
I realized that strength can't be given

00:22:40.690 --> 00:22:45.670
It's something I have to grab myself

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:51.110
In that case, I have to keep moving
I can't stay still

00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:56.370
Even if walls and headwinds block my way

00:22:56.570 --> 00:23:01.970
I'll draw my trump card called 
"courage" to take a step forward

00:23:01.970 --> 00:23:06.390
I believe in my story of victory

00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:12.360
Everyone during battle is My Way
Duelists are being tested

00:23:12.360 --> 00:23:17.770
When times are tough, that's when you 
Smile, Jump, Fight & Step Up!

00:23:17.770 --> 00:23:23.100
Your smile is your Energy
Kick away your feelings of running away

00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:32.410
Jump into the new field
Shiny One Step that leads to the future

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:40.660
One step... Just one step is fine
That's your Big Chance!!

00:23:46.130 --> 00:23:49.860
The tournament is finally starting!  
I'm gonna reach my dad's level!

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:53.360
I built the strongest deck, so I'll be fine!

00:23:53.360 --> 00:23:56.360
I'll show you my entertainment dueling!

00:23:56.360 --> 00:23:58.100
I'll make everyone shiver!

00:23:58.100 --> 00:24:01.800
I trained for this day!  I promise to win!

00:24:01.800 --> 00:24:06.200
Everyone, are you ready?  Let's 
do our best and win it all!

00:24:06.200 --> 00:24:07.600
Yeah!

00:24:07.600 --> 00:24:12.360
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V:
Maiami Championship Begins!!

00:24:12.360 --> 00:24:14.560
The fun is only getting started!
